# Security

## Trust boundaries

- Existing repository paths, documents, definition evidence, manifests, configuration, and metadata are untrusted input until validated.
- `audit` is deterministic read-only inventory and does not execute configured or detected project commands.
- Adoption writes only after a conflict-free audit and preserves existing authority outside bounded managed blocks.
- Commands committed in `dev/harness.toml` execute with the caller's environment and permissions.
- Git history and explicit base/head/target values provide local integrity evidence; they are not authorization.
